in main
  an owned string shortened to more than half of its block keeps it: True
  the same length keeps it too: True
  a write after it needs no copy: True
  a join reads only the length: True
  to half of it or less it moves to a block that fits: True
  a grow takes a new block and its new characters are zero: True
  a block of 32 bytes or less is kept however short: True
  shortened one at a time it always fits its block and ends in a small one: True
  a large block too: kept above half, left far below it: True
  a shared string shortened gets a block of its own: True
  so does the other holder: True
  a literal shortened is copied: True
  a view shortened is copied and its block never written: True
  an element, a field and a var parameter keep their blocks above half: True
  and leave them below it: True
  a join and a Copy are their own and keep theirs too: True
  shortened to nothing it is the empty string: True
  a read with room for 64 KiB keeps the block when it fills it, not when it is short: True
  a datagram of 4 bytes read with room for 64 KiB holds a small block: True
16 routines at once, every case held: True
